Spec: RunCmd

Platform: Rust

Purpose:
  Back the `agent run` sub-command: execute one Rhai script file standalone, with the
    script's own directory and the agent script library on the module search path. It is
    the developer-facing "run this script now" entry, outside any package lifecycle.

Exposes:
  @Parameters — clap `Args`, `Debug`; both fields private to this module.
  @run — validates the script path, builds the interpreter, executes the file.

Accepts:
  @Parameters.script — `-f` / `--file`, @env `SCRIPT`, value name `SCRIPT`, a @PathBuf.
  @Parameters.script_dir — `-s` / `--script-dir`, @env `SCRIPT_DIRECTORY`, value name
    `SCRIPT_DIRECTORY`, @PathBuf, clap @default_value `./agent/scripts` (a literal
    string, resolved relative to the process CWD at interpretation time).

Returns:
  @common::Result of @(): @Ok on a completed run; the @run_file error propagates via
    `?` otherwise.

Raises:
  @common::Error::MissingScript carrying the cloned @PathBuf — sole self-minted error,
    when @Parameters.script is not an existing regular file at check time (a directory
    or symlink-to-directory also fails @Path::is_file).
  Propagated @common::Error from @Script::run_file — parse or runtime failure inside
    the script, unmapped and unwrapped.

Handles:
  Script with no parent directory (a bare `foo.rhai` relative path yields `""` from
    @Path::parent fallback via @std::path::Path::new("")).
  @Err arm — ./main.sdd logs `{e:}` through @tracing::error and exits the process 1;
    nothing here calls @process::exit.

Must:
  Check @Path::is_file on the raw @Parameters.script before touching the interpreter;
    no search, no extension requirement, no readability probe.
  Build @common::rhaihandler::Script::new with exactly two search dirs in this order:
    the script's parent directory (@to_string_lossy), then
    `{script_dir}/lib` formatted via @PathBuf::display — the `lib` segment is appended
    by plain string concat, so a @script_dir ending in `/` yields a doubled separator.
  Discard @run_file's returned @Dynamic with `let _ =` while still propagating its
    @Err through `?`: script values are never observed, script failures always are.
  Emit no output of its own; all stdout/stderr comes from the script or logging.

Depends on:
  ../common/src/rhaihandler.sdd — @Script::new search-path semantics and @run_file.
  ../common/src/lib.sdd — @Error::MissingScript variant and its Display text.
  ./main.sdd — the only caller (`Run` dispatch arm, exit-1 error lane).

Scenario: missing script file
  Given `RunCmd` and @Parameters.script pointing at a non-existent path or a directory
  When @run is invoked
  Then @tracing::error logs `"{:?} is not a file"` with the path
  And @run returns @Error::MissingScript holding the same @PathBuf
  And no interpreter is constructed

Scenario: script runs with parent and lib dirs on the search path
  Given @Parameters.script naming an existing file `dir/app.rhai` and @script_dir `sd`
  When @run is invoked
  Then @Script::new receives search dirs `["dir", "sd/lib"]` in that order
  And a successful @run_file yields @Ok(()) regardless of the discarded @Dynamic

Scenario: script error propagates untouched
  Given @Parameters.script naming a file whose execution fails inside the interpreter
  When @run reaches `let _ = rhai.run_file(...)?`
  Then the @Err surfaces from @run unchanged for main's exit-1 lane

Tasks:
  [ ] Decide later whether the `let _ =` discard of the script's final value is wanted
      or the value should gate success/logging.
  [ ] Decide later whether @script_dir should be validated (exists, is a directory)
      before building the interpreter; today a wrong @script_dir only fails if the
      script actually imports from it.
  [ ] Cover the three scenarios with tests; `run.rs` has no `#[cfg(test)]` module and
      no test invokes @run.

Done when:
  The three scenarios hold under tests and the search-path order stays frozen.
